  "question": "For which value(s) of $k$ is the function $f(x) = \\begin{cases} kx^2, & x \\leq 1 \\\\ 2x-1, & x > 1 \\end{cases}$ continuous at $x=1$?",
  "answeroption": "A",
  "explanation": "Require $\\lim_{x \\to 1^-} f(x) = \\lim_{x \\to 1^+} f(x) = f(1)$.<br /><br />$\\lim_{x \\to 1^-} f(x) = k(1)^2 = k$<br /><br />$\\lim_{x \\to 1^+} f(x) = 2(1) - 1 = 1$<br /><br />So $k=1$",
